From: Husarion <support@husarion.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SHM: recovering a dead listener's buffers locks the port mutex once

When a sender finds a port marked not ok, SharedMemManager::Port::try_push()
regenerates it, and for a zombie port (its listener's process died) it first
runs recover_blocked_processing(), which calls
SharedMemGlobal::Port::get_and_remove_blocked_processing() until no listener
is marked as processing a buffer. That function holds the port's
empty_cv_mutex and calls listener_processing_stop(), which locks the same
non-recursive mutex again: the inner lock times out after
BOOST_INTERPROCESS_TIMEOUT_WHEN_LOCKING_DURATION_MS (1 s), its exception is
swallowed, the slot stays marked as processing, the function returns true,
and the loop calls it again, forever. A participant that died between taking
a message and finishing it leaves exactly such a slot, so the next sender to
regenerate its port spins in that loop holding the mutex, inside the send
path: the participant's send resources stay locked, nothing it publishes
reaches anyone, and its discovery listener blocks as soon as it has to send
or create sender resources, so it never follows the discovery port when the
other processes regenerate it. Present in 2.6.x, 2.14.x and 3.x.

get_and_remove_blocked_processing() now clears the flag under the lock it
already holds, and recover_blocked_processing() stops after one pass over the
listener table. Private headers only, no change to the shared-memory layout.

---
--- a/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemGlobal.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemGlobal.hpp
@@ -798,7 +798,9 @@
                             node_->listeners_status[i].is_processing)
                     {
                         buffer_descriptor = node_->listeners_status[i].descriptor;
-                        listener_processing_stop(i);
+                        // empty_cv_mutex is already held here: listener_processing_stop() would
+                        // lock it again, time out and leave the slot marked as processing.
+                        node_->listeners_status[i].is_processing = false;
                         return true;
                     }
                 }
--- a/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemManager.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemManager.hpp
@@ -929,7 +929,10 @@
             if (SharedMemGlobal::Port::is_zombie(global_port_->port_id(),
                     shared_mem_manager_->global_segment()->domain_name()))
             {
-                while (global_port_->get_and_remove_blocked_processing(buffer_descriptor))
+                // Each call clears one slot: one pass over the listener table is enough,
+                // and a bound keeps a slot that cannot be cleared from spinning forever.
+                for (uint32_t pass = 0; pass < SharedMemGlobal::PortNode::LISTENERS_STATUS_SIZE &&
+                        global_port_->get_and_remove_blocked_processing(buffer_descriptor); ++pass)
                 {
                     auto segment = shared_mem_manager_->find_segment(buffer_descriptor.source_segment_id);
                     if (!segment)
